TIP:  The double (D) chords on either side of “Sugar” and “Honey” and the (G) afterwards is necessary to keep the timing because of the unsung “do, do, do-do, do do” that goes between.

FUN FACT:  Sugar Sugar was co-written by Andy Kim who had hits with "Baby I Love You" and "Rock Me Gently."  Andy also accompanies lead singer Ron Dante on the song.  Believe it or not, Sugar Sugar spent four weeks at #1 and was the Single of the Year for 1969.  Groovy.
  
 
